A fine-tune checkpoint holds what training changed, the trainable weights and the buffers, and no longer the frozen pretrained weights, which come back with the model from its recorded checkpoint commit. A QLoRA checkpoint could not be restored: it held the 4-bit backbone, whose quantization entries `load_state_dict` rejects. LoRA and QLoRA checkpoints of REVE shrink to about 6 MiB. Restoring raises an error when the checkpoint lacks weights the model trains or holds weights the model does not have.
